Achmage Workbench — rhwp v0.9.0 form of a 0.8.7 engine patch (third_party/hop/patches-0.9.0).
Origin: HOP 0007 (third_party/hop/patches/0007-hop-widow-orphan-keep-next.patch, sha256 7c9340a3011867fcb9135b2c647650e63d1618efc76935d82f19884101630969; original author hop-workbench <hop@localhost>)
Status: ported
Differs from the 0.8.7 form: upstream applies widow/orphan only to endnotes, so nothing runs twice; widow_orphan is computed inside the split function; provenance field, section-flow and paragraph-flow hunks placed by hand; keep-with-next budget without the 0.8.7 footnote margin (0.9.0's split loop has none); drift-margin hunk not applied (0.9.0's margin is 0). The rules still apply only to sections with no stored lines, and 0.9.0 marks re-laid-out lines as stored, so a new document typed from the blank template does not get them.
Regression test: hop_rules::tests::widow_keeps_two_lines_together, orphan_moves_a_first_line_alone (brought by the patch); hop_0007_widow_moves_a_second_line_with_the_last, hop_0007_orphan_moves_a_paragraph_whose_first_line_ends_the_page, hop_0007_keep_with_next_moves_a_paragraph_to_its_successor (new, also with the rules off); H4b: upstream's passthrough guard (tests/issue_2724_passthrough_invalidation_guard.rs classification_drift_is_blocked) gets set_hop_pagination_rules as a SessionState exemption (a layout flag, no document change)

